# ── WP2C: spec/ is NOT excluded wholesale, because two files in it are RUNTIME
# DATA, not documentation. betting/pool_catalog.py opens
# spec/pool_catalog_rev1_3.json and spec/pool_stat_vocabulary_rev1_0.json at
# import time, so a deploy that dropped them would fail closed the moment the
# Pool catalog subsystem is reached.
#
# WHY PATTERNS RATHER THAN A NEGATION. `spec/` followed by
# `!spec/pool_catalog_rev1_3.json` does NOT work under gitignore semantics: once
# a directory is excluded, a later negation cannot re-include a file inside it,
# because the directory is never descended into. Relying on that would look
# correct in review and ship an empty spec/ directory. The exclusions are
# therefore written as explicit patterns that never exclude the two runtime
# files in the first place.
#
# The superseded catalog revisions are named individually rather than caught by
# a glob, so that adding a future revision is a deliberate decision about
# whether it is runtime data — the same exact-name convention .gitignore uses.
spec/*.md
spec/*.html
spec/pool_catalog_rev1_0.json
spec/pool_catalog_rev1_1.json
spec/pool_catalog_rev1_2.json
Architecture_Diagram_v12.html
green_*.txt
red_*.txt
